zed\":\"$undefined\"}]]}],{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"parallelRouterKey\":\"children\",\"error\":\"$undefined\",\"errorStyles\":\"$undefined\",\"errorScripts\":\"$undefined\",\"template\":[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{}],\"templateStyles\":\"$undefined\",\"templateScripts\":\"$undefined\",\"notFound\":\"$undefined\",\"forbidden\":\"$undefined\",\"unauthorized\":\"$undefined\"}]]}],{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"parallelRouterKey\":\"children\",\"error\":\"$undefined\",\"errorStyles\":\"$undefined\",\"errorScripts\":\"$undefined\",\"template\":[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{}],\"templateStyles\":\"$undefined\",\"templateScripts\":\"$undefined\",\"notFound\":\"$undefined\",\"forbidden\":\"$undefined\",\"unauthorized\":\"$undefined\"}]]}],{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[\"$L4\",[[\"$\",\"script\",\"script-0\",{\"src\":\"/_next/static/chunks/0xv9uz7g8af6d.js\",\"async\":true,\"nonce\":\"$undefined\"}]],[\"$\",\"$L5\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$6\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.MetadataOutlet\",\"children\":\"$@7\"}]}]]}],{},null,false,null]},null,false,\"$@8\"]},null,false,\"$@8\"]},null,false,\"$@8\"]},null,false,null],[\"$\",\"$1\",\"h\",{\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"$L9\",null,{\"children\":\"$La\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"hidden\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$6\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.Metadata\",\"children\":\"$Lc\"}]}]}],[\"$\",\"meta\",null,{\"name\":\"next-size-adjust\",\"content\":\"\"}]]}],false]],\"m\":\"$undefined\",\"G\":[\"$d\",[[\"$\",\"link\",\"0\",{\"rel\":\"stylesheet\",\"href\":\"/_next/static/chunks/0-7zhabl4g7ue.css\",\"precedence\":\"next\",\"crossOrigin\":\"$undefined\",\"nonce\":\"$undefined\"}]]],\"S\":true,\"h\":null,\"s\":\"$undefined\",\"l\":\"$undefined\",\"p\":\"$undefined\",\"d\":\"$undefined\",\"b\":\"CCxR80sZRnjlIdOoXSFK7\"}\ne:[]\n8:\"$We\"\nf:I[22016,[\"/_next/static/chunks/01xlw8hd842-c.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0d3shmwh5_nmn.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0xv9uz7g8af6d.js\"],\"\"]\n10:I[16505,[\"/_next/static/chunks/01xlw8hd842-c.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0d3shmwh5_nmn.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0xv9uz7g8af6d.js\"],\"LessonClient\"]\n11:T8d6,# Control Flow\n\nControl flow statements let you make decisions and repeat actions in your scripts.\n\n## if / elseif / else\n\nThe most fundamental decision structure. The condition must be wrapped in parentheses, and the body goes inside braces:\n\n```powershell\n$score = 85\n\nif ($score -ge 90) {\n    \"Grade: A\"\n} elseif ($score -ge 80) {\n    \"Grade: B\"\n} elseif ($score -ge 70) {\n    \"Grade: C\"\n} else {\n    \"Grade: F\"\n}\n```\n\n## switch Statement\n\nUse `switch` when comparing one value against many possibilities. It is cleaner than a chain of `if/elseif` blocks:\n\n```powershell\n$day = \"Monday\"\n\nswitch ($day) {\n    \"Monday\"    { \"Start of the week\" }\n    \"Friday\"    { \"Almost weekend!\" }\n    \"Saturday\"  { \"Weekend!\" }\n    \"Sunday\"    { \"Weekend!\" }\n    default     { \"Midweek day\" }\n}\n```\n\n> **Key Concept:** Unlike many languages, PowerShell's `switch` tests **every** case by default and does not fall through. Use `break` inside a case to stop after the first match.\n\n## foreach Loop\n\nIterates over each item in a collection:\n\n```powershell\n$fruits = @(\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\")\n\nforeach ($fruit in $fruits) {\n    \"I like $fruit\"\n}\n```\n\n## for Loop\n\nA counted loop with an initializer, condition, and increment:\n\n```powershell\nfor ($i = 0; $i -lt 5; $i++) {\n    \"Iteration $i\"\n}\n```\n\n## while and do-while / do-until\n\n**`while`** checks the condition before each iteration:\n\n```powershell\n$count = 0\nwhile ($count -lt 3) {\n    \"Count is $count\"\n    $count++\n}\n```\n\n**`do-while`** always executes at least once, then checks:\n\n```powershell\n$input = \"\"\ndo {\n    $input = Read-Host \"Enter 'quit' to exit\"\n} while ($input -ne \"quit\")\n```\n\n**`do-until`** runs until the condition becomes true (the inverse of `do-while`):\n\n```powershell\n$num = 1\ndo {\n    $num *= 2\n} until ($num -ge 100)\n```\n\n## break and continue\n\n**`break`** exits the current loop entirely. **`continue`** skips the rest of the current iteration and moves to the next:\n\n```powershell\nforeach ($n in 1..10) {\n    if ($n -eq 3) { continue }  # skip 3\n    if ($n -eq 7) { break }     # stop at 7\n    $n\n}\n# Output: 1 2 4 5 6\n```\n\n> **Key Concept:** `break` and `continue` work in `foreach`, `for`, `while`, `do-while`, and `do-until` loops. Inside a `switch`, `break` exits the switch statement.\n4:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"min-h-screen bg-zinc-950 text-zinc-100\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"header\",null,{\"className\":\"sticky top-0 z-10 border-b border-zinc-800/60 bg-zinc-950/80 backdrop-blur-xl\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto flex max-w-4xl items-center justify-between px-6 py-3.5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$Lf\",null,{\"href\":\"/module/fundamentals\",\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-zinc-500 transition-colors hover:text-zinc-300\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"h-4 w-4\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"d\":\"M10.5 19.5L3 12m0 0l7.5-7.5M3 12h18\"}]}],\"PowerShell Fundamentals\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$Lf\",null,{\"href\":\"/module/fundamentals/operators-and-comparisons\",\"className\":\"flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-zinc-800 text-zinc-400 transition-colors hover:border-zinc-700 hover:text-zinc-200\",\"title\":\"Operators and Comparisons\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"h-4 w-4\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"d\":\"M15.75 19.5L8.25 12l7.5-7.5\"}]}]}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs tabular-nums text-zinc-500\",\"children\":[5,\" / \",9]}],[\"$\",\"$Lf\",null,{\"href\":\"/module/fundamentals/functions-and-parameters\",\"className\":\"flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-zinc-800 text-zinc-400 transition-colors hover:border-zinc-700 hover:text-zinc-200\",\"title\":\"Functions and Parameters\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"h-4 w-4\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"d\":\"M8.25 4.5l7.5 7.5-7.5 7.5\"}]}]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 pb-4\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"h1\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight\",\"children\":\"Control Flow\"}]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L10\",null,{\"lesson\":{\"meta\":{\"title\":\"Control Flow\",\"description\":\"If/else, switch, foreach, and while loops.\",\"slug\":\"control-flow\",\"order\":5,\"prerequisites\":[\"m1-l4\"]},\"content\":\"$11\",\"exercises\":[{\"id\":\"m1-l5-ex1\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write an if/elseif/else block that checks the variable $score: if $score is greater than or equal to 90, output \\\"A\\\"; elseif $score is greater than or equal to 80, output \\\"B\\\"; else output \\\"F\\\".\",\"hints\":[\"Start with if ($score -ge 90) { ... }\",\"Follow with elseif ($score -ge 80) { ... }\",\"End with else { ... }\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"if\\\\s*\\\\(\\\\s*\\\\$score\\\\s+-ge\\\\s+90\\\\s*\\\\)\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Start with: if ($score -ge 90)\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"elseif\\\\s*\\\\(\\\\s*\\\\$score\\\\s+-ge\\\\s+80\\\\s*\\\\)\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Add: elseif ($score -ge 80)\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"else\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Include an else block for the default case.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"[\\\"']A[\\\"']\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Output \\\"A\\\" for scores >= 90.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"[\\\"']B[\\\"']\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Output \\\"B\\\" for scores >= 80.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"[\\\"']F[\\\"']\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Output \\\"F\\\" for the else case.\"}],\"solution\":\"if ($score -ge 90) {\\n    \\\"A\\\"\\n} elseif ($score -ge 80) {\\n    \\\"B\\\"\\n} else {\\n    \\\"F\\\"\\n}\",\"explanation\":\"The if/elseif/else chain evaluates conditions top to bottom and executes the first block whose condition is $true. The else block runs when no conditions match.\"},{\"id\":\"m1-l5-ex2\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write a switch statement that checks the variable $status. If \\\"Running\\\", output \\\"Service is active\\\". If \\\"Stopped\\\", output \\\"Service is inactive\\\". Include a default case that outputs \\\"Unknown status\\\".\",\"hints\":[\"Syntax: switch ($variable) { 'value' { action } }\",\"Use 'default' for the fallback case.\",\"Remember to include the curly braces around each action.\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"switch\\\\s*\\\\(\\\\s*\\\\$status\\\\s*\\\\)\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Start with: switch ($status)\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"[\\\"']Running[\\\"']\\\\s*\\\\{\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Add a case for \\\"Running\\\" with a script block.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"[\\\"']Stopped[\\\"']\\\\s*\\\\{\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Add a case for \\\"Stopped\\\" with a script block.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"default\\\\s*\\\\{\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Include a default case for unmatched values.\"}],\"solution\":\"switch ($status) {\\n    \\\"Running\\\" { \\\"Service is active\\\" }\\n    \\\"Stopped\\\" { \\\"Service is inactive\\\" }\\n    default { \\\"Unknown status\\\" }\\n}\",\"explanation\":\"The switch statement compares $status against each case. The default block runs when none of the cases match, similar to else in an if statement.\"},{\"id\":\"m1-l5-ex3\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write a foreach loop that iterates over the array $names and outputs \\\"Hello, <name>\\\" for each element. Use the loop variable $name.\",\"hints\":[\"Syntax: foreach ($item in $collection) { ... }\",\"Use double quotes for string expansion: \\\"Hello, $name\\\"\",\"The loop variable is $name and the collection is $names.\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"foreach\\\\s*\\\\(\\\\s*\\\\$name\\\\s+in\\\\s+\\\\$names\\\\s*\\\\)\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use: foreach ($name in $names)\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"[\\\"']Hello,\\\\s*\\\\$name[\\\"']\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Output \\\"Hello, $name\\\" inside the loop body.\"}],\"solution\":\"foreach ($name in $names) {\\n    \\\"Hello, $name\\\"\\n}\",\"explanation\":\"The foreach loop assigns each element of $names to $name in turn, then executes the script block. Double-quoted strings expand $name to its current value.\"},{\"id\":\"m1-l5-ex4\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write a for loop that counts from 1 to 5 (inclusive) and outputs each number. Use $i as the loop variable.\",\"hints\":[\"Syntax: for ($i = start; $i -le end; $i++) { ... }\",\"Start at 1 and go up to 5 using -le.\",\"Output $i inside the loop body.\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"for\\\\s*\\\\(\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Start with the for keyword followed by parentheses.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\$i\\\\s*=\\\\s*1\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Initialize $i to 1.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\$i\\\\s+-le\\\\s+5\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Continue while $i is less than or equal to 5.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\$i\\\\+\\\\+\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Increment $i with $i++ in the for statement.\"}],\"solution\":\"for ($i = 1; $i -le 5; $i++) {\\n    $i\\n}\",\"explanation\":\"The for loop has three parts in its parentheses: initialization ($i = 1), condition ($i -le 5), and increment ($i++). The body executes as long as the condition is $true.\"},{\"id\":\"m1-l5-ex5\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write a foreach loop over the numbers 1 to 10 that uses 'continue' to skip even numbers and 'break' to stop when the number reaches 8. Use $n as the loop variable and 1..10 as the range.\",\"hints\":[\"Use $n % 2 -eq 0 to check for even numbers.\",\"Put 'continue' inside an if block to skip even numbers.\",\"Put 'break' inside an if block to stop at 8.\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"foreach\\\\s*\\\\(\\\\s*\\\\$n\\\\s+in\\\\s+1\\\\.\\\\.10\\\\s*\\\\)\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use: foreach ($n in 1..10)\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"continue\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use 'continue' to skip even numbers.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"break\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use 'break' to stop the loop at 8.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\$n\\\\s*%\\\\s*2\\\\s*-eq\\\\s*0\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Check for even numbers with: $n % 2 -eq 0\"},{\"rule\":\"order\",\"sequence\":[\"foreach\",\"continue\",\"break\"],\"hintOnFail\":\"Place 'continue' (skip evens) before 'break' (stop at 8) in the loop body.\"}],\"solution\":\"foreach ($n in 1..10) {\\n    if ($n % 2 -eq 0) { continue }\\n    if ($n -eq 8) { break }\\n    $n\\n}\",\"explanation\":\"The 'continue' keyword skips the rest of the loop body for even numbers, jumping to the next iteration. The 'break' keyword exits the loop entirely when $n reaches 8. Only odd numbers 1, 3, 5, 7 are output.\"}],\"moduleSlug\":\"fundamentals\"}}],\"$L12\"]}]\n12:[\"$\",\"footer\",null,{\"className\":\"border-t border-zinc-800/60\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto flex max-w-4xl items-center justify-between px-6 py-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$Lf\",null,{\"href\":\"/module/fundamentals/operators-and-comparisons\",\"className\":\"group flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-zinc-400 transition-colors hover:text-zinc-200\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"h-4 w-4 transit